From: Iscandar build <iscandar@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0008] iscandar: register caches at do_kmem_cache_create

Third and fourth kernel-round boots (2026-11-22): with
0007 in, KR4 reached ready with no engine findings, then
cache creations failed ENOMEM one after another (a dma
cache, iommu_iova, uid_cache with SLAB_PANIC) and the
boot panicked. The failing allocations never reached
iscandar_alloc: the door's registry lookup returned 0
and slab_alloc_node returned NULL before any counter
moved, which is why the log is silent after ready.
Cause, from the tree: patch 0003 hooked registration at
the end of __kmem_cache_create_args, but kmem_cache,
kmem_cache_node, and the whole kmalloc family are born
by create_boot_cache, which calls do_kmem_cache_create
directly and never passes create_args. Those caches
were never registered, and after ready every allocation
from them met the lookup-0 finding. The coverage audit
enumerated the allocation doors but not the cache birth
paths; this is the birth path it missed. Fix: register
at the out point of do_kmem_cache_create, the one
function both birth paths pass (its error path already
releases the cache, so a cap refusal unwinds the same
way), remove the create_args hook, and follow the two
boot caches across bootstrap(), where the cache changes
identity from the boot static to a heap struct: the
registry is updated to name the live pointer. Desk
check: mm/slub.o and mm/slab_common.o compile clean on
the 0007 stack.

---
--- a/mm/slab_common.c
+++ b/mm/slab_common.c
@@ -377,17 +377,10 @@
 		}
 		return NULL;
 	}
-	/* Register before the cache is returned to its
-	 * creator: an unregistered cache must never reach
-	 * 1.1. Registration runs in every state (the
-	 * registry is mass memory beside the doors; there
-	 * is no raise to defer it to). A refusal is the
-	 * cap's verdict: the creation fails, loudly. */
-	if (iscandar_cache_register(s, object_size,
-				    args->align, flags)) {
-		kmem_cache_destroy(s);
-		return NULL;
-	}
+	/* Registration itself lives at the end of
+	 * do_kmem_cache_create, the one point every
+	 * cache birth passes, boot-born and general
+	 * alike (patch 0008). */
 	if (!iscandar_active())
 		iscandar_prefix_note(ISCANDAR_CENTER_CACHE_SETUP,
 				     object_size);
--- a/mm/slub.c
+++ b/mm/slub.c
@@ -6035,6 +6035,15 @@
 #endif
 	}
 	list_add(&s->list, &slab_caches);
+	/* The cache changes identity here: the registry
+	 * holds the boot static's name from its creation.
+	 * Follow the identity across: unregister the
+	 * static, register the live cache. */
+	iscandar_cache_unregister(static_cache);
+	if (iscandar_cache_register(s, s->object_size,
+				    s->align, s->flags))
+		panic("iscandar: registry refused bootstrapped cache %s\n",
+		      s->name);
 	return s;
 }
 
@@ -6183,6 +6192,24 @@
 		debugfs_slab_add(s);
 
 out:
+	if (!err)
+		/* Every cache birth in the tree passes this
+		 * point: the general path through create_cache
+		 * and the boot path through create_boot_cache
+		 * alike. Register here, before the cache is
+		 * returned to its creator, so no live cache is
+		 * ever unregistered. (The hook patch 0003
+		 * placed at the end of __kmem_cache_create_args
+		 * never saw the boot-born caches: kmem_cache,
+		 * kmem_cache_node, and the whole kmalloc
+		 * family are born by create_boot_cache, and
+		 * every allocation from them after ready met
+		 * lookup 0 and returned NULL, KR4, 2026-11-22.)
+		 * A refusal is the cap's verdict: the
+		 * creation fails through the same release
+		 * path as any other error. */
+		err = iscandar_cache_register(s, s->object_size,
+					      s->align, s->flags);
 	if (err)
 		__kmem_cache_release(s);
 	return err;
